# Line endings.
#
# The repo is edited on Windows but deployed to Linux. Git's autocrlf can turn
# LF into CRLF on checkout, and a shell script or systemd unit that arrives with
# \r\n fails on the server with "$'\r': command not found" — which is a
# confusing failure to debug at deploy time. Pin these to LF in the repository
# so it cannot happen no matter what any machine's autocrlf is set to.
*.sh            text eol=lf
*.service       text eol=lf
*.yml           text eol=lf
*.yaml          text eol=lf
*.py            text eol=lf

# Excel workbooks are committed (they are read at runtime) and must never be
# line-ending-normalised or merged as text.
*.xlsx          binary
*.docx          binary
*.pbix          binary
